WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.174 line:74%
Copilot Fusion is generally
available: for every request,

2
00:00:04.174 --> 00:00:09.081 line:74%
Copilot picks the models and, when
needed, makes them work together

3
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.035 line:74%
Rather than choosing a model for
every task,

4
00:00:13.035 --> 00:00:16.597 line:74%
you let Copilot Fusion decide,
request by request,

5
00:00:16.597 --> 00:00:19.731 line:74%
which models to use and how to
combine them;

6
00:00:19.731 --> 00:00:23.578 line:74%
the user sets the effort level:
Standard, High or Max.

7
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.827 line:74%
Depending on the task: a single model
handles it directly; or,

8
00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:33.610 line:74%
in cascade mode, a cheaper model
drafts and a quality check decides

9
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:38.037 line:74%
whether to keep the answer or move up
to a stronger model; or,

10
00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:41.750 line:74%
in critique mode, one model drafts,
another reviews,

11
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.677 line:74%
then the first one revises.

12
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.612 line:74%
Other clients aren’t supported yet
(announced as “coming soon”,

13
00:00:48.612 --> 00:00:52.659 line:74%
with no date); each model used is
billed at its standard rate.
